WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.400
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.400
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.400
<b>Only for the Summer
 Ankoro</b>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.020
They're done.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.260
Please evaluate them.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.530
Good enough.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.250
Thank you so much.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.410
Hey, Itsuka! Where should we go next?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.190
How about Hirakata Park?

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.460
They've got a ride called 
Pachanga that's really popular!

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.950
What are you doing?

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.790
Mom! Look!

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.590
This shot came out really well!

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.680
The one where Itsuka is really cute, right?

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:34.120
You've already shown me so many times.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.780
Hmm?

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.960
There's an old guy in there.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.010
That's me!

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:38.990
Oh, that's right!

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.050
We have to go pick up the flowers.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:42.170
Saki-kun?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:43.450
Yes, ma'am?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.520
I'm sorry. Can I ask you to go?

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.880
I'll go right away.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.400
I'll go with you.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.730
Thanks.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.130
Then should I go, too?

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.180
You don't have to come, Nagomu-san.

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:55.140
It's because you're an old man.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.440
Seriously, can't you do my birth over 
again? Make me a pretty lady instead!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:08.790
<b>Recipe for
 Happiness</b>

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:36.380
<b>A Blue Wind Rustling Fresh Leaves</b>

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.460
Since then, she won't even answer me anymore.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:37.870
What do I do?

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:40.680
Asking me when you're already 
in a stalemate is...

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.420
But, Saki-kun, you get 
along with her so well!

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.710
Like today, you went on that errand together!

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.270
That was just her helping me out, that's all.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:51.440
But "helping out" is something you 
don't do unless there's trust, right?

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.730
<i>I can't tell if his bar is set high or low.</i>

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:55.930
I was wondering...

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:00.300
Nagomu-san, you started training so 
you could inherit Ryokushou, right?

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:05.050
Well... Dad wants to ask Itsuka to do it,

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.800
so I can't really speak up about it.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.960
What about you, Saki-kun?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.360
Your family runs a manju shop, right?

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.880
Um, yes.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.400
Then your family must feel relieved.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.170
I mean, you're skilled at 
everything you do, Saki-kun.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:22.620
I studied sweets and went to university.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.930
Once I'd graduated, I asked 
to start training right away.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:28.580
Though it's my older brother 
who'll take over our family shop.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:37.440
<b>Yasugiri Foods</b>

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:37.440
<b>Kyoto</b>

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:37.440
<b>Dainagon Azuki Beans</b>

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:35.000
Ever since I was little, I've been told, 
"Let's work together to take care of our shop,"

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.440
so I am planning to help 
support my brother, but...

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.200
Nagomu!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.010
Huh?

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.490
What have you done now?!

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.470
What's the meaning of Tsukiyama-san's 
household canceling their order?!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.990
What?!

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:52.860
I'm so sorry.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.880
I know that visiting after you've 
told us we didn't have to is rude,

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.310
but if my idiot son has done 
something wrong, that's a big problem.

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:03.470
No, it's nothing like that.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:04.340
What?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.600
You know that we host classes 
at our house every week?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.320
Generally, I serve as the host,

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.700
but lately I've been entrusting 
them to my son, too.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:15.440
I see.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:20.090
My son was supposed to 
host next week's class,

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:24.440
but he's suddenly started 
saying that his "heart hurts."

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:27.920
When I asked, he said he'd fallen 
in love at first sight...

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:30.780
with a girl who seems to work at Ryokushou.

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:32.110
So...

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.450
Excuse me for interrupting.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.710
I've brought tea.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.640
Thank you.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.530
This is my son, Tadashi.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.220
They came from Ryokushou.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.430
What did you come here for?!

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:53.400
Have you decided to tell me about the girl?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.650
You're just going to 
refuse again, aren't you?

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.210
I just want to treasure this 
fluttering feeling of being in love!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:05.120
Until these wounds in my heart heal, I won't
 have anything to do with your sweets!

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:06.550
Please leave!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:11.040
I'm so sorry.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.160
He gets very emotionally fragile 
when he doesn't get his way.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:18.840
It's fine. But when he said 
"the girl," was that...

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.920
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.760
Thank you!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.050
When our sweets were delivered,

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:29.300
a—smartphone, I think you call it?—
was left behind.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.040
And when he looked at the lock screen...

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.230
It seems that the girl 
he saw there was lovely.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:37.000
He asked who it was, but...

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.270
he said the person refused to tell him.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.340
To think my son is doing this when 
he should be holding a class.

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:46.700
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.700
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:45.660
I can't apologize enough.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.760
I'm so sorry!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.450
What's already done can't be helped.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.020
After hearing the reason, 
everything makes sense.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.960
It's happened before, too.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:59.800
Love affairs have made him say he'd 
quit school, or quit tea ceremony.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.420
He's caused a lot of trouble.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:03.380
He sounds like a complicated boy.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.270
That's all fine.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:09.590
But the girl in the photo... 
It wasn't Itsuka, was it?

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.640
I'm back!

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.020
Did you just call my name?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.890
Welcome home!

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.710
This girl?

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.000
Oh, no, she's doesn't work at Ryokushou!

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.570
You're better off giving up on her!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.530
<i>You wouldn't be a good match for her!</i>

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.810
<i>I didn't mean to speak that way.</i>

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.660
Oh, she's cute.

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.800
But she sort of looks like Saki-kun somehow.

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.330
Wha?!

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.010
Why do you have that?!

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.510
Well, it was just sitting there.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.920
Is it your little sister? Wait.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.960
But, Saki-kun, you only have 
an older brother, right?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:46.800
Is she your cousin?

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.370
That's...

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.970
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:50.220
What?

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:53.610
If you keep pestering him, 
he'll start hating you, you know?

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.870
Huh? No way. I'm sorry.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:03.980
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:03.980
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.980
It's been a few days since then.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:06.760
Saki-kun seems to have lost all his energy.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.150
Well, he feels like he's destroyed our 
relationship with a regular customer.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.580
Young master, why don't you try 
inviting him out for a drink?

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.360
Yeah, I should.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:20.190
He's probably got things it would be easier 
to talk with you about than with us.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:23.750
<b>Sanjo-kobashi</b>

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.120
I see.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.800
I guess I should go find a place that 
seems easy to have a conversation in.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.140
Huh?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.830
Wait...

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.930
That girl is...

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:36.260
She's the one from his lock screen!

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.020
<b>We'll Find the Person You Want to See</b>

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.770
And now, we've finally found her!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.720
Tsukiyama Tadashi-san!

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:44.810
At long last...

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.920
you meet, face-to-face!

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:50.460
Congratulations!

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.740
May there be happiness for 
you as you set out together!

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.730
<i>Ryokushou-san, we'd like to be 
your regular customers again!</i>

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:57.860
That's it!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.940
Excuse me!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.280
Are you alone?

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:06.040
Will you let me buy you a drink?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.250
I'm not anyone suspicious. I'm actually...

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.260
Huh?

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.590
Oh no!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.070
I think I might have left 
the gas on in the workshop!

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.430
That's terrible!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.740
If you don't check that properly, you...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.740
For real?

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.850
Ever since I was little,

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:33.450
there's been stuff about my family, 
my brother, my parents' expectations...

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.320
I had nowhere to escape to.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.780
<b>Zaimoku
 Bridge</b>

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.780
<b>Minami-Daikokubashi Street</b>

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:42.540
Then, while I still wasn't sure what I 
wanted to do, when I went to university...

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.900
I was in a cross-dressing 
café for a school festival.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.540
And it made me feel light, 
like everything was easier.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:53.380
So, it's become a habit to do 
this when stuff goes wrong.

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:57.140
I shouldn't have made the 
photo my lock screen.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:02.780
But having it there... every time I see it,
 I remember there's another me...

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.760
and it makes me feel calmer.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.270
But I won't do this anymore.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.930
Itsuka-chan has been helping me with things.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.880
Huh? Wait! She knows?!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:15.900
Yes.

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:20.280
I dropped my makeup kit in 
front of Itsuka-chan once.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:21.790
Since then, she's known.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:25.500
She said, "There must be places it's 
hard for a guy to go into alone,"

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.120
and she's been going with me 
to those places to buy things.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.600
I'm sorry. I'll go now.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.000
Wait.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:37.930
The way you look right now...

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.340
You can draw a line under things. How about it?

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:48.690
An order?

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.390
Well, if there's a request, 
I'll make it, but...

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:52.960
It seems a little suspicious.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.570
No, no! It isn't anything strange!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.840
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:00.080
<i>I didn't think my everyday actions 
would affect things like this!</i>

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.860
I'm the one who asked for it.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:07.090
But I thought it would seem strange 
for a child to place an order.

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:08.490
Please, will you do it?

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:11.310
Well, I guess I've got no choice.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.090
You're not even asking her for a reason!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:18.590
Are you sure about this? If he 
finds out, he'll be angry with you.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.050
If I hadn't stepped up, your whole 
plan would have fallen apart there.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:25.110
That's what happens when someone 
untrustworthy tries to do things.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.590
This is for Saki-kun, right?

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:31.160
It's not like I've got no connection to this.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.170
I-Is this real?

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.840
Um, I saw a photo of you and—

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:46.520
Shh!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.550
A letter?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.920
W-Wait!

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.180
At least tell me... your name.

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.300
<i>Excuse my abruptness.</i>

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:09.480
<i>I heard that you've been looking for me.</i>

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.850
<i>Thank you.</i>

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:17.990
<i>And I apologize for the rude way 
my cousin Saki spoke to you.</i>

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:24.380
<i>Tsukiyama-sama, I am engaged to be married.</i>

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.080
<i>In the summer, the green maple 
leaves are called "kaede,"</i>

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.300
<i>In the fall, they change colors, 
turning crimson, and become "momiji."</i>

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:36.280
<i>As you think of their transformation, 
I hope you will understand.</i>

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:44.230
The flower language of kaede is "restraint," 
"self-control," and "precious memories."

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.700
And the taste...

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:48.220
is sweet...

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.960
and heartbreaking.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.100
Sweets don't just express the seasons.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.970
They can also represent 
scenes and emotions.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.310
There's no limit to what they can express.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:07.120
Though both the giver and the 
receiver have to do their research.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.840
In that case, the fact that 
you wrote that letter...

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:13.900
must mean that you've done a whole lot 
of research on women's hearts, right?

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.860
Say, Saki-kun.

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:23.700
I have a favor to ask.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.850
<b>Traditional Confectionery</b>

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.850
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:28.490
I'm back!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.310
If a young man doesn't work for you, then how
 would you feel about a young lady?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.870
Stop being stupid and go 
make these deliveries!

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:39.500
Right away!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.030
<b>Only for the Summer
 Ankoro</b>

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.030
<b>Ryokushou</b>

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:45.860
<b>Beating the Summer Heat</b>

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.160
It's so hot.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:52.480
Was Kyoto always this hot?

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:55.290
Nagomu! Stop cooling off and get to work!

00:12:56.790 --> 00:12:58.220
They're ready!

00:12:58.220 --> 00:12:59.640
I'll take them.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.220
For table three, right?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:03.300
Yeah.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.620
Thanks!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.910
What is it?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:13.390
<b>Don't forget to
wash your hands
and gargle!</b>

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:10.490
Oh, it's nothing.

00:13:10.490 --> 00:13:12.860
Then please don't create awkward pauses.

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:15.340
You'll make me think I got the order wrong.

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:20.020
<i>Her verbal sparring is 
the same as ever, but...</i>

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:24.740
<i>I feel like she's a little 
softer than before.</i>

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.280
<i>What I don't understand now is...</i>

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.820
Hello!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:32.040
Welcome, Kanoko-chan!

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.940
I'm here on an errand.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.810
You're working hard.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:41.100
I've heard from everyone at Kafuuen 
that you're being very helpful.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:44.840
Not at all. I'm still not used to 
things, so I'm only causing problems.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.120
I'm sure that's not true!

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:49.400
<i>She came here from Tokyo for some 
sightseeing and then settled down here.</i>

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:49.770
When you helped out here, you 
were so adept at everything!

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:53.840
<i>After dumping me, she must not 
think anything of me at all.</i>

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.420
Oh, no, really...

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:53.840
Hello, Itsuka-chan.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:55.560
Hello, Kanoko-san!

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.030
What will you have?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.280
Well...

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:01.860
Could I please have ten ankoro mochi?

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.320
<b>Ankoro</b>

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.320
<b>piece</b>

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.320
<b>yen</b>

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.320
<b>yen</b>

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.320
And...

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:06.570
could you tell that person over 
there that he's being creepy?

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:08.700
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:13.200
Ankoro mochi is something you have on 
the midsummer day of the ox, right?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.130
It's also called doyou mochi, 
or "midsummer mochi,"

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:17.020
and it's said to help beat the summer heat.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:20.330
It's one of the sweets that has 
been beloved since long ago.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:25.580
Our manager said that there's no surviving 
the summer without eating them.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:27.720
Oh, that's right!

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.430
<b>Valid for 7/1~8</b>

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:31.430
<b>Aqua Athletic Park Pool</b>

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:31.430
I was told to give these to Itsuka-chan.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:34.040
Oh, they're complimentary tickets to a pool.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:36.930
I'd like to take you,

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:40.940
but it wouldn't be any fun if you 
went with someone as old as me.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:45.100
And my husband's hurt his back, 
so he's getting a massage on his day off.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.760
I see.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:50.030
I know! Kanoko-chan! Won't you take her?

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:50.950
What?

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:54.010
Kafuuen is closed on the 
same days we are, after all.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:56.370
If you're all right with me taking her.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:57.920
Hold on!

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:02.280
There's another healthy 
adult over here, you know?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.890
<b>Aqua Athletic Park Pool</b>

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.880
We're here!

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.360
We'll see you in a minute.

00:15:15.360 --> 00:15:16.550
Sure thing.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.600
<b>Men's Changing Room</b>

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:19.600
But...

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:22.100
Was it really okay for me to come with you?

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:25.710
More than that, I want 
to thank you for coming.

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:27.580
If it were just Itsuka, 
that would be one thing.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:29.440
But going to the pool with my 
ex-girlfriend is a little...

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.820
Then wouldn't it have been 
better if you didn't come?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.740
It's a free ticket to a pool!

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.500
It's hot every day! I want 
to go to the pool, too!

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:39.790
Yes. Of course.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.290
While we're waiting for them to join us,

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:46.700
let's go over there to the racing area!

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.610
Oh...

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.650
Maybe after I've gotten a little 
more used to the water...

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.450
Then let's jump in here first!

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.230
Huh? Wai—!

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.820
Sorry. I can't.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.020
Are you serious?

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:11.110
There you are.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.160
What are you doing?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.910
Well, that's...

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.640
Nagomu, you're going over there, right?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:20.910
<b>Exciting!
 Kid's Pool</b>

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.910
Stop talking like I've 
always used the kid's pool!

00:16:21.260 --> 00:16:24.670
I'll look after everyone's stuff. 
You three should go have fun.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.070
Well then, thanks!

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.750
Wow, the ground's really hot! Let's 
hurry up and get in over there.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:31.930
All right!

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:40.170
I won't be using it, 
so I'll let you borrow it.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:42.060
Thank you!

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:44.950
I'm going now.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:05.460
<i>Hmm?</i>

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.390
<i>It must be coming from that stage.</i>

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:11.100
<i>Now that I think about it...</i>

00:17:11.550 --> 00:17:14.810
<i>I haven't really played guitar lately.</i>

00:17:14.810 --> 00:17:17.370
<i>I do clean it every day, but...</i>

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:23.390
Nagomu, the sweat and oil from 
your hands will rust the strings.

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:24.980
So you have to be careful of that.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:27.800
<i>Senpai...</i>

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.750
<i>I wonder how he's doing.</i>

00:17:31.220 --> 00:17:33.720
<i>He taught me how to play guitar.</i>

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:35.950
<i>And he formed a band with me.</i>

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.950
<i>He used to come over to hang out a lot, too.</i>

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.100
Nagomu.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.140
I'm leaving Kyoto.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:49.500
It's time you decided your future, too.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.030
<i>See you around.</i>

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:57.140
<i>I mean, he could have at least 
left me a way to contact him.</i>

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:00.910
Huh? Where are the other two?

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.210
They're in a line with a 20-minute wait.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.890
I'll get burned standing 
under this blazing sun,

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.790
so I'm taking a break.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:16.150
<b>Aqua Athletic Park Pool</b>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:16.150
<b>On the Right</b>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:16.150
<b>Welcome!</b>

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:16.150
<b>Fuuen no Yu</b>

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:14.140
Oh, there's an onsen near here. 
Let's stop by on the way back.

00:18:14.140 --> 00:18:16.150
I don't mind, but...

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.850
What? You're being creepy.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:20.950
It's just...

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:24.490
Why did you come to Kyoto?

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.830
And decide to live here, too.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.060
What you're doing seems pretty reckless.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:34.390
I told you. The timing all worked.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:40.010
I found a place to work, and our manager 
showed me a place I could live.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:44.010
Everything I needed to start 
something new just lined up for me.

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.760
It was the same for you, wasn't it? 
You came back because the timing was right.

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:52.020
Well, when you put it 
like that, you're right, but...

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:55.100
I feel like you're trying 
to skip past something.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:56.140
Really?

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.460
Where to next?

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:03.260
Um, Saki-kun...

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:07.000
Hey.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.290
Hmm?

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.410
Are you not going to even 
touch the guitar anymore?

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:15.630
No, I touch it every day. And I practice
 the hand motions for playing.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.250
But my fingers start 
rotating before I know it.

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:19.380
They what?

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.400
It's called "houan."

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:27.310
<b>Houan</b>

00:19:21.400 --> 00:19:24.030
And it's one of the basics of making wagashi.

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:27.310
You practice the motion using 
round objects, clay, or similar things.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.550
And you're saying you end up doing that.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:30.310
That's right.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.930
I understand.

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:34.870
Understand what?

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:38.100
Oh, the other two are back!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.700
Are you having fun?

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:41.980
Yes.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:45.200
If you're having fun, then everything's great.

00:19:49.440 --> 00:19:50.670
Nagomu-san!

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:52.650
Let's head to the water slides next!

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.350
Even someone who sinks like
 a stone can handle those.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.880
Don't be so blunt about it!

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:59.300
"Let's do something that 
Nagomu-san can do, too."

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:02.010
It was Itsuka-chan's suggestion.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.370
Do you want to refuse?

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:06.970
Of course I'm going!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.210
Time waits for no one, you know?

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.470
Why are you so excited all of a sudden?

00:20:11.470 --> 00:20:13.870
You're in fine form today.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:14.690
Huh?

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:17.080
Huh?

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.120
Itsuka!

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:23.420
Coming!

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:32.620
<b>Summer Vacation
Aqua on Stage</b>

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:28.540
<i>That was Karashi, a local band!</i>

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.420
<i>Thank you for your performance!</i>

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:37.130
<b>Karashi</b>

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:37.130
Man, thanks so much for helping 
us out by playing today.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:37.170
<b>Honorarium</b>

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:37.290
<b>Honorarium</b>

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:37.420
<b>Honorarium</b>

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.670
<b>Honorarium</b>

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:39.670
Sorry for calling you out at the last minute.

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:42.730
You really saved us, Yukihira.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.940
<b>Men's Changing Room</b>

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:01.940
Ow...

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.880
It stings so much.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.410
That's what happens when you get cocky.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.160
<b>Women's Changing Room</b>

00:21:06.980 --> 00:21:08.670
Oh no.

00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:11.160
I got a little burned.

00:21:11.160 --> 00:21:13.240
And I was being careful, too.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.740
No one will notice that.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:18.830
You think so? Well, I suppose 
a little burn isn't too bad.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:20.250
It'll make a good memory, right?

00:21:23.320 --> 00:21:26.330
Kanoko-san, are you all right?

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:27.460
With what?

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:31.000
Having the person who dumped you so nearby...

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.860
Isn't it exhausting?

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:40.400
Well, it can't be the same 
as it was before, but...

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:44.250
Now that I've seen him earnestly 
trying to do what he can...

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:46.570
It's made me want to watch over him.

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:52.490
It'd be nice to use "like" or 
"hate" to have a clean break,

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:54.010
but sometimes the more you learn,

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:57.180
the harder it is to tidy away 
a relationship like that.

00:21:57.660 --> 00:21:59.420
Even when you aren't related by blood.

00:22:01.120 --> 00:22:04.120
Do you understand Nagomu a little better now?

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:07.610
Someone who sinks like a stone is a little...

00:22:07.610 --> 00:22:10.140
Oh, I know, right?

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:14.430
Now that I think about it, there wasn't 
anything to add to the "plus" column.

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:17.130
Will you be able to go in the onsen?

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:19.540
It might be... rough.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:51.570
<b>Omikuji</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:24:10.050
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:50.030 --> 00:24:10.050
<b>"Welcoming the Spirits"</b>

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.360
"The person you're waiting for 
is running a little late."

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.120
I love it.

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:58.410
What a coincidence. So do I.

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.120
We're just the same!

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:02.210
G-Grandma!

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:04.750
You must protect the flavors of Ryokushou.

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:06.590
That's your job.

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:07.880
Who are you again?

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.050
Your grandson, Nagomu!
